scsi: no uevent for a power-on or reset unit attention, as LG's 4.4 kernels

LG's 4.4 kernels (webOS 5 and 6; N21D's has no SDEV_UA=POWER_ON_RESET_OCCURRED)
send no uevent for a power-on or reset unit attention (29/xx); this kernel
sends one, a scsi_device change. QEMU's emulated USB stick reports that
unit attention on its first command, and webOS's 60-block.rules forwards
the change to the disk, where udev rebuilds the disk's database entry
without the properties LG's rules set only on add (READ_ONLY, CARD_READER,
HARD_DISK). PDM's start scan then takes a stick present at power-on as
removed and never mounts it. Do as LG's 4.4 kernels do: send no
uevent (the warning stays).

--- a/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
@@ -516,7 +516,12 @@
 		}
 
 		if (sshdr->asc == 0x29) {
-			evt_type = SDEV_EVT_POWER_ON_RESET_OCCURRED;
+			/*
+			 * No uevent (SDEV_UA=POWER_ON_RESET_OCCURRED): LG's 4.4
+			 * kernels have none, and webOS's 60-block.rules turns it
+			 * into a block "change" that drops the add-only udev
+			 * properties PDM's start scan needs (READ_ONLY).
+			 */
 			/*
 			 * Do not print message if it is an expected side-effect
 			 * of runtime PM.
